+/* Winamp (VC142) uses the C11 threads layer from MSVCP140. The recompiled
+ * guest is single-threaded/cooperatively scheduled, so its mutexes and
+ * condition variables need no host synchronization; a no-op that leaves the
+ * (zeroed) guest object alone is enough for the calls to return. */
